From 7a5552c72e3a5e314981a2875c59e8f74a9b6f2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:56:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Tamer looks: backpacks in sixteen colours on every shirt,
 chosen on the Look page

A backpack is a garment with no objects: one sector of TAMER.DAT with its drawing, its palette recipe and its
polygons, which the loader copies into the room every shirt but the original keeps in its torso. Those shirts
carry a second drawing of the trunk with a backpack's straps, used unless the backpack is none. The original
hoodie has its backpack in its mesh: with another backpack or none the loader reads one of two shirts that are
not chosen from, the same hoodie without it. The shoes' first sector is read once more for a boot's leg, the
backpack's having taken its place.

The choices are eleven bytes (save record 0x000F as it is, longer); the Look page has eleven rows, its two
hints over and under the button that opens it. The tamer's choices are no longer cleared when the scripts
start: the program's memory is cleared before that, and a save load clears them itself.
